\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i\b0\loch
Gi\u7919\'3f \u273\'3f\u250\'fang m\u7885\'3fi th\u244\'f4ng s\u7889\'3f k\u7929\'3f thu\u7853\'3ft c\u361\'3f (2 cm, 0\u176\'b0/180\u176\'b0, 1 pt / 2 pt, #000000 / #FFFFFF, layer LASER CUT, Laser Cut t\u7855\'3ft m\u7863\'3fc \u273\'3f\u7883\'3fnh, kh\u244\'f4ng t\u7921\'3f l\u432\'3fu); b\u7887\'3f thu\u7853\'3ft ng\u7919\'3f n\u7897\'3fi b\u7897\'3f; th\u234\'eam 'Common problems' v\u224\'e0 'What to read next'.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf22\f5\fs28\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Getting Started with Nova Nesting in Illustrator}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i\b0\loch
URL: /tools/nest-pro/articles/getting-started}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Nova Marker Making and Nesting works on the Illustrator file you already have open. This guide covers what to prepare, what to set, and what to check before you save.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
1. Put patterns inside the artboard and designs outside it}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Open your Illustrator document and make the artboard that holds your pattern pieces the active artboard. Keep the pattern outlines inside it: they must be visible, unlocked, closed paths with no fill. Place the matching designs outside the artboard. Hidden or locked objects are skipped, and you do not need to select anything by hand.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
2. Check the matching tolerance}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
The matching tolerance is set to 2 cm by default. Nova Nesting uses it to compare the width and height of each design with each pattern piece, then compares area, proportions and outline shape. Leave it at the default for your first run and change it only if your pieces call for it.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
3. Decide whether you need Laser Cut}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Laser Cut is optional and is OFF by default. Leave it off to match and align only. Turn it on if you also want laser strokes created around each placed design.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
4. Set the laser output, if you turned it on}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Inside Stroke defaults to 1 pt and Outside Stroke to 2 pt. Each stroke has its own color picker, with black (#000000) for the inside stroke and white (#FFFFFF) for the outside stroke by default. The strokes go on a layer named LASER CUT. Use a layer that holds nothing else, because the selected layer is cleared before new strokes are created.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
5. Run Nova Nesting}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Nova Nesting finds the pattern piece that fits each design, keeps the design at 0\u176\'b0 or turns it exactly 180\u176\'b0, and moves your existing artwork so its center sits on the center of the matched pattern. The artwork is moved, not copied. Each pattern piece is used only once per run.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
6. Review the result, then save}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Check the summary of placed designs and failures, and look at the artboard itself. Nova Nesting never saves or exports on its own, so save the Illustrator file yourself once you are happy with it.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Common problems}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
A design was not placed: check that it sits outside the active artboard and that it is visible, unlocked and filled. A pattern piece was not found: check that its outline is closed, has no fill and sits inside the active artboard. A design went to the wrong piece: read How Silhouette Matching Works, then review the tolerance and the shapes. Strokes are missing: confirm that Enable Laser Cut is checked.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
What to read next}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Continue with the Nesting + Laser Cut workflow for the full sequence, or Set Inside and Outside Laser Strokes if your job needs laser output.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf22\f5\fs28\b\dbch\af8{\loch
How Silhouette Matching Works in Nova Nesting}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i\b0\loch
URL: /tools/nest-pro/articles/how-silhouette-matching-works}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Nova Nesting pairs each design with a pattern piece by comparing shapes in stages. It has one matching method, not separate Quick Scan and High Performance Scan modes.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
1. It narrows the candidates by size}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
For each design, Nova Nesting first keeps only the pattern pieces whose width and height are within the matching tolerance (2 cm by default). It then compares aspect ratio and area. This skips clearly unsuitable pairs before the detailed comparison.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
2. It compares the outline shape}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
The pieces that remain are compared by the shape of their outline, using a normalized fingerprint of each path, and by the difference in perimeter. The fingerprint is also checked after a 180\u176\'b0 turn, so a design that fits better upside down is recognized.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
3. It chooses 0\u176\'b0 or 180\u176\'b0}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
If the 0\u176\'b0 comparison is the better fit, the design stays as it is. If the 180\u176\'b0 comparison is better, the design is turned exactly 180\u176\'b0. No other angles are used.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
4. It uses each pattern piece once}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Once a pattern piece is matched, it is marked as used for the rest of the run, so two designs are never placed on the same piece.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
5. Laser Cut is a separate step}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Matching and placement come first. After that, the Enable Laser Cut option decides whether the inside and outside strokes are created. It is OFF by default.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
If a design is matched to the wrong piece}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Look at the tolerance, and at whether two pieces have very similar outlines. Check that every pattern outline is closed, has no fill and sits inside the active artboard, and that every design sits outside it. Always inspect the artboard before production; Nova Nesting does not replace your own check.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
What to read next}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
See the Nesting + Laser Cut workflow for the order of every step, or go back to Getting Started.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf22\f5\fs28\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Nesting + Laser Cut Workflow in Illustrator, Step by Step}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i\b0\loch
URL: /tools/nest-pro/articles/nesting-workflow}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
This is the exact order Nova Nesting follows, from the file you prepare to the result you save. Laser Cut is optional and can be skipped.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
01 / Prepare the file}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Open the Illustrator file and make the pattern artboard active. Keep closed, unfilled pattern outlines inside it and filled design artwork outside it. Hidden and locked objects are skipped.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
02 / Set the options}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Set the matching tolerance (default 2 cm). Laser Cut starts OFF. If you turn it on, the panel offers an Inside Stroke of 1 pt, an Outside Stroke of 2 pt, black and white colors, and the LASER CUT output layer.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
03 / Scan and match}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Nova Nesting reads the pattern outlines and the design silhouettes, using the clipping path when artwork is clipped. It filters by size, aspect ratio and area, then compares shape and perimeter. A pattern piece cannot be used twice in one run.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
04 / Orient and align}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
The design stays at 0\u176\'b0 or is turned exactly 180\u176\'b0, depending on the match. Your existing artwork is moved so its center sits on the center of the matched pattern; it is not duplicated.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
05 / Optional laser strokes}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
If Enable Laser Cut is checked, the selected output layer is cleared and separate inside and outside strokes are created from each successfully placed design. The strokes follow the design silhouette, not the pattern outline.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
06 / Review and save}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Check the counts of placed designs, failures and strokes, then inspect colors, widths, layer order and geometry on the artboard. Nova Nesting does not save or export anything. Save the file yourself.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
What to read next}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Read How Silhouette Matching Works for the logic behind step 03, or Set Inside and Outside Laser Strokes for step 05.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af11\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf22\f5\fs28\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Set Inside and Outside Laser Strokes in Illustrator}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i\b0\loch
URL: /tools/nest-pro/articles/laser-stroke-output}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Laser Cut adds inside and outside strokes around each placed design. Turn it on only when the job needs laser output.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Laser Cut is off by default}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
The Enable Laser Cut checkbox is unchecked when you start. While it stays off, Nova Nesting matches and aligns your designs and creates no strokes.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Set the stroke widths}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
When Laser Cut is on, the Inside Stroke is 1 pt and the Outside Stroke is 2 pt by default. Enter positive widths that suit your workflow.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Choose the stroke colors}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Each stroke has a color picker that shows its hexadecimal value. The defaults are black (#000000) for the inside stroke and white (#FFFFFF) for the outside stroke.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Use a dedicated LASER CUT layer}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
The output layer is named LASER CUT by default. Before the new strokes are created, anything already in the selected layer is cleared. Keep unrelated artwork out of it.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Layer order and source shape}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
White is placed underneath black by default. The strokes are made from each successfully placed, closed design silhouette. The pattern outline is not the source.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
Check before you cut}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Look at the geometry, colors, stroke widths and layer contents on the artboard. Nova Nesting does not save or export automatically, so save the file yourself before it goes to the cutter.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\rtlch\af11\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb200\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf24\f5\fs24\b\dbch\af8{\loch
What to read next}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Go to the Nesting + Laser Cut workflow to see where this step fits, or back to Getting Started.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af11\afs28\ab \ltrch\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\keep\widctlpar\sb480\sa0\keepn\ltrpar\cf22\f5\fs36\b\dbch\af8{\loch
8. FAQ trang ch\u7911\'3f (b\u7843\'3fn \u273\'3fang ch\u7841\'3fy)}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
What is Nova Nesting?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Nova Nesting is a set of production tools for apparel makers. It includes Nova Marker Making and Nesting for Adobe Illustrator and NOVA Trame for Adobe Photoshop.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
What does Nova Nesting do in Illustrator?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
It compares each design on your artboard with the pattern outlines, finds the matching pattern piece, keeps the design at 0\u176\'b0 or turns it exactly 180\u176\'b0, and aligns it in place. The existing artwork is moved, not copied. Laser cut strokes are optional.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
Does Nova Nesting save or export my file automatically?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
No. Nova Nesting never saves or exports on its own. Review the placement and the summary, then save the file yourself.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
What is NOVA Trame?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
NOVA Trame is a Photoshop plugin with 130 halftone styles for DTF printing on black and white shirts. The dot frequency (LPI) is set from your print size, and a live preview shows the result before you apply it.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
Can I try the tools before I buy?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Yes. Both tools start with a 7-day free trial, so you can test them on your own patterns and artwork.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033{\loch\i0\b\loch
How do I get help?}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af11\afs22\alang1025 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af5\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\f5\fs22\cf0\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar{\loch\i0\b0\loch
Read the step-by-step guides, or email support@ainovanesting.pro. License periods, prices, refund policy and terms are listed on the site.}
